---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Colophon — how this site is built"
  description="How edwardchapman.co.uk is built: Astro on Cloudflare Pages, agentic toolchain, CI-gated."
>
  <main>
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <p class="muted">How this site is built — because the how is the point.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Static by design.</strong> Built with
        <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, deployed on Cloudflare Pages.
        There is no origin server — the previous incarnation of this domain died
        with one, and this one structurally can't.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Built with an agentic toolchain.</strong> Scaffolded and maintained
        with <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code">Claude Code</a>
        running my own
        <a href="https://github.com/edjchapman/claude-code-config"
          >claude-code-config</a
        > kit — vendored CI workflows, commit standards, validation hooks. The tooling
        works because it's constrained: every change lands through a PR gated by
        <code>make check</code> (format, type check, production build) and a strict
        commit-style validator.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Machine-readable.</strong>
        <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> summarises the site for AI agents. An interactive,
        eval-gated "ask about my work" agent is in the works — grounded strictly on
        this site's published content, with an LLM-as-judge harness in CI so answer
        quality is measured, not assumed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open.</strong> The
        <a href="https://github.com/edjchapman/edwardchapman.co.uk">source</a> is
        public — repo standards, workflows and all.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </main>
</Base>
